 "الفرق بين: Error / Warning / Exception": "The difference: Error / Warning / Exception",
 "Error = حاجة وقفت البرنامج. Warning = تحذير والبرنامج كمّل. Exception = خطأ وقت التشغيل تقدر «تمسكه» (catch) بـ try/except.": "Error = something stopped the program. Warning = a caution, and the program carried on. Exception = a run-time error you can “catch” with try/except.",
 "DeprecationWarning: this function will be removed in version 3.0\n→ لسه شغال، بس غيّره قريب": "DeprecationWarning: this function will be removed in version 3.0\n→ still works, but change it soon",
 "أفعال بتوصف اللي حصل": "Verbs that describe what happened",
 "raise/throw = رمى خطأ. catch/handle = مسك الخطأ وتعامل معاه. fail = فشل. crash = وقع فجأة. hang/freeze = علّق. time out = خلص وقته.": "raise/throw = produce an error. catch/handle = grab the error and deal with it. fail. crash = stop suddenly. hang/freeze = get stuck. time out = run out of time.",
 "اسأل عن الخطأ صح": "Search for the error the right way",
